Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:01:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: an audio driver on libSceAudioOut

Audio out on libSceAudioOut's main port, in two buffers: 48 kHz, 16-bit or
float samples, mono, stereo or 7.1 (in SDL's channel order), from 256 to
2048 samples a buffer. A 7.1 port the system will not open falls back to
stereo. The SDK has no link stubs for libSceAudioOut, so the driver loads
it with libSceSysmodule when it starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018H1dHz3GdyTDdPL1TtZf9k
